{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetProlongation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetProlongation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Generators"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.pentagon_inter_level_placeholder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.pentagon_inter_level_placeholder","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L276-L295","doc":"Forward-declaration placeholder (kept for backward compatibility\nwith downstream code that hypothesised against this name during\nPR #506). New code should hypothesise against `InterLevelLift`\ninstead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.pentagon_inter_level_on_transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.pentagon_inter_level_on_transient","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L248-L272","doc":"Pentagon UV-commutation on the transient block.\n\nSpecialised consequence of `q_graded_commutation`: when `R_q`\nvanishes (e.g., on the transient summand `B_λ^trans = ker τ̂_n`,\nwhere the descended part is by definition zero), the q-graded\nidentity simplifies to the pure quantum-torus relation\n`u·v = q·v·u`.\n\nThis is the **clean inter-level pentagon** statement that the\nnarrative `prop:pentagon-uv-commutation` Step 4 isolates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.q_graded_commutation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.q_graded_commutation","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L228-L228","doc":"The q-graded inter-level commutation identity. For\n`i, j, k : Generator n` (necessarily i < j < k for non-trivial\nordering), the operator-lift product\n  `u = Ũ_i ∘ Ũ_j` (composition lifted to End_C(A_{n+1}))\n  `v = Ũ_k`\nsatisfies `u · v = q · v · u  +  R_q`, where `R_q ∈ im τ̂_n` (i.e.\nis fixed by the descent involution).\n\nThis is the Step-3-and-4 content of\n`prop:pentagon-uv-commutation`'s narrative derivation: braid\nrelation + Hecke quadratic + descent splitting on the q-eigenblock.\n\nStated as the existence of `R_q` with the divisibility-by-descent\nproperty so that any concrete instance only needs to exhibit the\noperator-lift action and verify the residual is descended. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.liftOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.liftOperator","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L212-L212","doc":"Per-jet-level operator lift `Ũ_ℓ : EndAlg n → EndAlg (n+1)`,\none for each braid-generator index `ℓ : Generator n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.mk","kind":"ctor","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.toJetChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift.toJetChain","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L204-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.InterLevelLift","kind":"class","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L182-L238","doc":"**Inter-level pentagon ascension** — operator-lift typeclass +\nsubstantive theorem.\n\nFor a triple `(i, j, k)` of braid-generator indices and the\noperator-lift `Ũ_ℓ : EndAlg n →ₗ[R] EndAlg (n+1)` carrying the\nquantum-torus structure, the level-internal product\n`u = Ũ_i Ũ_j` and `v = Ũ_k` satisfy\n`u · v = q · v · u + R_q` where `R_q ∈ im τ̂_n` is the descended\nresidual (i.e., is fixed by the descent involution).\n\nThis is `prop:pentagon-uv-commutation`'s **inter-level lift**\ncontent. The level-internal version (single jet level n) is plain\ncommutativity in the scalar trace ring; see\n`QOU.BraidKnot.VhatPairCommutationTrace`.\n\nThe typeclass `InterLevelLift` packages the operator lift `Ũ_ℓ`\ntogether with the q-graded commutation identity as fields. A\nconcrete instance for the Hecke chain awaits the substantive\nbrane-tower / `H_n(q) → H_{n+1}(q)` quantum-torus implementation,\nbut downstream theorems can already be stated and proved\n**conditionally** on `InterLevelLift` — making this typeclass the\nclean assumption point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.transientPart_isTransient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.transientPart_isTransient","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L168-L180","doc":"The transient part of an element is transient (lies in `ker τ̂_n`).\n\nProof: `τ̂_n (x − τ̂_n x) = τ̂_n x − τ̂_n² x = τ̂_n x − τ̂_n x = 0`,\nusing idempotency of `τ̂_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descendedPart_isDescended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descendedPart_isDescended","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L160-L166","doc":"The descended part of an element is descended (lies in `im τ̂_n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L154-L158","doc":"Every `x ∈ EndAlg (n+1)` decomposes as `x = descended + transient`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.transientPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.transientPart","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L150-L152","doc":"The transient part of an element: `x − τ̂_n x ∈ ker τ̂_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descendedPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descendedPart","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L145-L148","doc":"The descended part of an element under the descent-involution\nprojection: `τ̂_n x ∈ im τ̂_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.isTransient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.isTransient","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L141-L143","doc":"An element is **transient** if it lies in the kernel of `τ̂_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.isDescended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.isDescended","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L136-L139","doc":"An element of `EndAlg (n+1)` is **descended** if it lies in\nthe image of `τ̂_n` (equivalently, in the image of `ℓ_n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descentInvolution_idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descentInvolution_idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L120-L134","doc":"The descent involution is idempotent.\n\nProof: `τ̂_n² = ℓ_n ∘ 𝔡_{n+1} ∘ ℓ_n ∘ 𝔡_{n+1}\n             = ℓ_n ∘ (𝔡_{n+1} ∘ ℓ_n) ∘ 𝔡_{n+1}\n             = ℓ_n ∘ id ∘ 𝔡_{n+1}\n             = τ̂_n`,\nwhere the inner `𝔡_{n+1} ∘ ℓ_n = id` is the retraction identity\n(`descent_ascent`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descentInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descentInvolution","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L115-L118","doc":"The descent involution `τ̂_n = ℓ_n ∘ 𝔡_{n+1}` at level `n+1`.\nAn idempotent endomorphism of `EndAlg (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descent_ascent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descent_ascent","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Retraction identity: descending an ascended endomorphism\nrecovers it. Equivalent to `ℓ_n` embedding `A_n` as a direct\nsummand of `A_{n+1}` (Frobenius non-degeneracy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.descent","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Descent retraction at level n+1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.ascent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.ascent","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Ascent at level n: post-composition by `ℓ_n` lifts an\nendomorphism at level `n` to one at level `n+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.JetChain","kind":"class","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/JetProlongation.lean#L72-L106","doc":"**Jet prolongation chain** at a given category `C` over a base\nring `R`: an indexed family `A_n : ℕ → C` with ascent embeddings\n`ℓ_n : A_n ⟶ A_{n+1}` and descent retractions\n`𝔡_{n+1} : End(A_{n+1}) →ₗ[R] End(A_n)` satisfying the retraction\nidentity `𝔡_{n+1} ∘ post(ℓ_n) = id` (descending an ascended\nendomorphism recovers it).\n\nThe \"endomorphism algebra at level n\" is parameterised by an\nabstract `R`-module `EndAlg n`; the descent retraction is a linear\nmap between these. Concretely (e.g. for the Hecke chain) `EndAlg n`\nwould be the algebra `End_C(A_n)`; here we keep it abstract so the\ntypeclass is reusable for both the categorical brane tower and the\nalgebraic Hecke-chain instantiation.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b, this is a structural typeclass; substantive\nproofs at instances are deferred until concrete chains are wired\nup. The fields encode the **algebraic content** of the chain\n(idempotent decomposition, retraction identity); category-level\ncontent (objects, morphisms) lives in\n`lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation.lean`.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}